---
source: crates/roadbook-compiler/tests/fail.rs
---
error[RB0118]: `kids` is a children collection: say which child to send to
  --> RB0118-not-a-collection.road:19:52
   |
19 |     on Go     spawn kids[event.id] = Child()  send kids.Ping
   |                                                    ^^^^
   |
   = help: send to one child with `send kids[key].Ping`, or to every child with `send kids.*.Ping`

error[RB0118]: `one` names an invoked machine, not a children collection
  --> RB0118-not-a-collection.road:20:8
   |
20 |     on one.done -> A
   |        ^^^
   |
   = help: an invoked child is reached with `send one.Event` and `on one.Event`, and its outcome is handled inside its `invoke { }`

error[RB0118]: `peer` is a parameter or variable, not a children collection
  --> RB0118-not-a-collection.road:22:22
   |
22 |   on kids.Pong  stop peer[1]
   |                      ^^^^
   |
   = help: `stop peer` needs a collection declared in the machine body: `children peer: Machine by Key`

error[RB0118]: `n` is a parameter or variable, not a children collection
  --> RB0118-not-a-collection.road:23:6
   |
23 |   on n.done     send peer["x"].Ping
   |      ^
   |
   = help: `on n.done` needs a collection declared in the machine body: `children n: Machine by Key`

error[RB0118]: `peer` is not a children collection, so it takes no key
  --> RB0118-not-a-collection.road:23:27
   |
23 |   on n.done     send peer["x"].Ping
   |                           ^^^
   |
   = help: send to it with `send peer.Ping`

error[RB0118]: unknown children collection `kid`
  --> RB0118-not-a-collection.road:24:6
   |
24 |   on kid.fail * send kids.*.Ping
   |      ^^^
   |
   = help: did you mean `kids`?
